# Changing this file and pushing the change starts the "Search states" workflow for every state
# (see .github/workflows/search-states.yml); the Actions tab's "Run workflow" button can also
# choose states. Each run searches ONE topic: the one on the last "topic:" line, a [topics.NAME]
# of automation/govbooks.toml. Its results go to the sheet's "States - <topic>" tab.
# Requests:
# 2026-09-28 immigration, 5 books per state of 18+ pages, 37 states, covers and years, newest first
# 2026-09-30 tenant-landlord (ran together with immigration: mixed results)
# 2026-10-01 law-enforcement-careers (ran together with the other two: mixed results)
# 2026-10-03 tenant-landlord alone, 5 books per state of 18+ pages (counted pages only)
topic: tenant-landlord
